slipcase-common (1.1.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Five payload families, so that a container named for its payload draws with
    a mark for it: PDF, document, image, audio and video, each a subclass of
    application/x.slipcase+zip with its own glob list and its own drawing. A
    payload on no list keeps the plain icon and needs no declaration.
  * The icon is a guess from the container's name. SPEC Appendix B is
    non-normative and SPEC 3 forbids a reader to use it, so a wrongly named
    container draws the wrong mark. The products opening it say what is really
    inside. README argues why this is the trade to make rather than shipping a
    thumbnailer, which SPEC 6 describes as a hazard.
  * Each family names the plain icon as its generic-icon, so a family declared
    before its drawing exists degrades to the case rather than to a blank page.
  * slipcase-desktop and slipcase-open name all six types in their desktop
    entries. sub-class-of carries the default application but not the
    recommended list, which is matched on the exact type, so a family left out
    of a MimeType= line still opens but drops out of the top of Open With.
  * The package now carries this changelog under usr/share/doc, compressed,
    which policy 12.7 requires and lintian reported the absence of as an error
    in 1.0.0 as well.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 23:37:00 +0000

slipcase-common (1.0.0) stable; urgency=low

  * First release. The media type and its icon, taken out of the products that
    used to carry them so that one package owns them.
  * Breaks and Replaces slipcase-desktop before 0.1.3, which is where the icon
    moved out of. Without them dpkg refuses this package on any machine already
    carrying one of those versions.
  * The icon is declared twice in the media type, as the icon and as the
    generic icon. Without the second declaration a container draws as a blank
    generic document: GTK searches theme-major, and Adwaita answers
    application-x-generic before hicolor is reached.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Sun, 31 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0000
